judgements.notes:
I read both evidence files in full, with addendum §4-5 first. I verified these on the web:
- Wake Lock works in iOS home-screen apps from 18.4 (MDN browser-compat-data WakeLock.json). evidence-max wrongly calls this unverified.
- WebKit bug 215884 is marked RESOLVED (Feb 2026), found through search results. The tracker itself is blocked by the proxy.
- Azure pronunciation-assessment latency is about 2 s typically, with a reported tail of about 5% at around 20 s (github.com/Azure-Samples/cognitive-services-speech-sdk/issues/1327, JS SDK 1.18-1.19, 2021; current behaviour unverified). No design plans for slow tail responses in the UX. All should add a 'still checking… skip / keep going' state and a timeout, not only an 8-15 s hard timeout.
- learner-ux's Claude API prices match Anthropic's cached pricing table.

Through the learner lens, the best final design combines these:
- learner-ux's fixed Hear → Say → Use → Wrap ritual, trust ladder and adherence toolkit (backup if-then plan, pause mode, weekly review);
- lean-mvp's build order and adherence gates (an offline listening slice in about 2-3 weeks; 'fix friction before adding modules') and its French-bullet retell cards;
- evidence-max's listening-only session mode and its French ASR listener game in noise, with one-cue French feedback;
- measurement's neutral 'no verdict' handling, with validation moved out of learner sessions into developer batches.

Watch for:
- /h/ or any contrast running 4 weeks straight (boredom);
- 30-s final retell rounds (recycling);
- counting sessions under 5 minutes toward the target without a dose check;
- any design that makes corrective speaking feedback depend on recruiting human listeners.

Sources: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/main/api/WakeLock.json ; https://github.com/Azure-Samples/cognitive-services-speech-sdk/issues/1327 ; https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=215884 (status via search results).
